      "artist": "Cornellrockey04",
      "description": "Cochise County Courthouse — Bisbee, Arizona.\nfrom google search:\nOn August 3, 1931, Governor George W. P. Hunt dedicated the new courthouse constructed on Quality Hill in Bisbee. Two large copper-sheathed doors give entry to the lobby, which is paneled with Tennessee pink marble and trimmed with Belgian black marble. The building has terrazzo floors and staircases, mahogany trim, and brass stair railings throughout. This structure continues to serve the county today, housing three of the six divisions of the superior court, the office of the clerk of the superior court, and the offices and departments of the court administrator.",
